==============================================================================
ML_assignment_P26AI0008.ipynb - final saved run log
==============================================================================

This file contains the printed outputs stored in the committed
notebook ML_assignment_P26AI0008.ipynb (top to bottom), so the
final numbers are readable without launching Jupyter. The same
outputs can be regenerated with ./reproduce.sh full (about 2-4
hours on a laptop CPU).

Random seed: 260008 (roll number P26AI0008). Dataset: scikit-learn
Olivetti faces, split 240 train / 80 val / 80 test (6/2/2 per identity),
stored in data/olivetti_split.npz.

Dependency note: the committed figures were rendered with
matplotlib 3.8.2. The saved split, all Q1 results and all five
figures were re-verified to reproduce exactly on Linux with numpy
1.26/2.1, scikit-learn 1.3/1.4/1.5 and matplotlib 3.8/3.9; the
boosting accuracy tables reproduce exactly within one environment
and can drift by a few hundredths on a different OS/BLAS stack (see
README.md, 'Determinism').


